PTLib 2.12-beta10 (OPAL stack): include <termios.h> instead of <termio.h>

glibc 2.42 removed the legacy System V <termio.h> header, so this translation
unit does not compile on any host carrying it.  <termios.h> is the POSIX
replacement, and this file references only struct termios.  Unlike the 2.10.9
branch the guard here has no __GLIBC_ typo, so on Linux the include really is
compiled and the build really does fail without this change.

Applies to: 10503462abe31a6c288a39f6f894a5ceb367abbc (branch v2_12)
Upstream:   https://git.code.sf.net/p/opalvoip/ptlib

diff --git a/src/ptlib/unix/pipechan.cxx b/src/ptlib/unix/pipechan.cxx
index 00610c4..1e9c278 100644
--- a/src/ptlib/unix/pipechan.cxx
+++ b/src/ptlib/unix/pipechan.cxx
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
 #include <signal.h>
 
 #if defined(P_LINUX) || defined(P_SOLARIS)
-#include <termio.h>
+#include <termios.h>  /* glibc >= 2.42 removed the legacy <termio.h> */
 #endif
 
 #include "../common/pipechan.cxx"
